\import{fdip-macros}
\meta{agent-authored}{true}
\tag{fdip}
\taxon{Example}
\title{Two identical spin summands}
\date{2026-11-26}

\p{Take two copies of the circle carrier in \ref{fdip-016Q} and
let the direction and grading act on each copy by the same
operators. Exchanging the copies commutes with the direction
and the grading. Every word in the chosen lifts preserves each
copy, so the exchange is outside the group even though it fixes
the direction by conjugation. To determine which words in the
generators fix all directions, one can first multiply the
symbols subject to their relations.}
